{
  "company": "CRONUS International Ltd.",
  "messageType": "Inventory.PhysInventory.PreviewPost",
  "status": "Success",
  "contract": "json",
  "format": "chapters",
  "catalogue": {
    "name": "Inventory.PhysInventory.PreviewPost",
    "isEnabled": false,
    "filterTableNo": 233,
    "description": "Previews posting a physical inventory journal: returns the ledger entries it would create, then rolls everything back.",
    "selectionDescription": "Identify one existing nonrecurring Phys. Inventory journal batch using templateName/batchName or subject TEMPLATE|BATCH or SystemId. All supplied selectors must agree.",
    "messageDirection": "Inbound",
    "keywords": [
      "preview physical count posting",
      "preview count journal",
      "count journal ledger entries",
      "simulate stock take posting"
    ],
    "chargeable": true
  },
  "chapters": {
    "envelope": {
      "subject": {
        "use": "optional",
        "forms": [
          "TEMPLATE|BATCH",
          "systemId"
        ],
        "description": "Identifies the journal batch as TEMPLATE|BATCH, or as the SystemId of the Item Journal Batch. Without a subject, send templateName and batchName in data. Every selector that is sent must name the same batch."
      },
      "dataRequired": false,
      "version": "1.0",
      "contentType": "text/json"
    },
    "target": [
      {
        "source": "subject",
        "form": "TEMPLATE|BATCH",
        "description": "The journal template name and the batch name, each at most 10 characters, separated by a vertical bar. The template must be a Phys. Inventory template that is not recurring."
      },
      {
        "source": "subject",
        "form": "guid",
        "description": "The SystemId of the Item Journal Batch."
      },
      {
        "source": "data.templateName, data.batchName",
        "form": "journal template and batch name",
        "description": "The template and the batch together. data.journalTemplateName and data.journalBatchName are accepted as aliases."
      }
    ],
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "templateName",
        "type": "string",
        "required": false,
        "description": "Name of an existing Phys. Inventory journal template that is not recurring, at most 10 characters. Send it with batchName unless subject identifies the batch."
      },
      {
        "name": "batchName",
        "type": "string",
        "required": false,
        "description": "Name of an existing journal batch of that template, at most 10 characters. Every selector that is sent must name the same batch."
      },
      {
        "name": "journalTemplateName",
        "type": "string",
        "required": false,
        "description": "Alias of templateName. A value that differs from templateName, ignoring case, is refused."
      },
      {
        "name": "journalBatchName",
        "type": "string",
        "required": false,
        "description": "Alias of batchName. A value that differs from batchName, ignoring case, is refused."
      },
      {
        "name": "lineSystemIds",
        "type": "array",
        "required": false,
        "description": "Nonempty array of distinct SystemIds of journal lines in the selected batch. Only those lines are used. Omit it to use every line of the batch."
      }
    ],
    "response": {
      "contentType": "text/json",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "status",
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Success when the preview ran and captured entries."
        },
        {
          "name": "templateName",
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The journal template of the selected batch."
        },
        {
          "name": "batchName",
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The selected journal batch."
        },
        {
          "name": "linesToPost",
          "type": "integer",
          "description": "Number of selected lines in the preview."
        },
        {
          "name": "rollback",
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "Always true: the preview entries were rolled back."
        },
        {
          "name": "preview",
          "type": "array",
          "description": "The captured entries, one object per table.",
          "children": [
            {
              "name": "tableId",
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Number of the table of the entries."
            },
            {
              "name": "tableName",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Name of the table."
            },
            {
              "name": "tableCaption",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Caption of the table."
            },
            {
              "name": "entryCount",
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Number of entries captured for the table."
            },
            {
              "name": "entries",
              "type": "array",
              "description": "The captured entries with their main fields."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "totals",
          "type": "object",
          "description": "G/L totals of the preview: totalDebitLCY, totalCreditLCY and, only when G/L entries were captured, balanced."
        },
        {
          "name": "result",
          "type": "array",
          "description": "The selected lines that were previewed.",
          "children": [
            {
              "name": "systemId",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "SystemId of the journal line."
            },
            {
              "name": "lineNo",
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Line number in the batch."
            },
            {
              "name": "itemNo",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Item number of the line."
            },
            {
              "name": "quantity",
              "type": "decimal",
              "description": "The adjustment quantity of the line."
            },
            {
              "name": "locationCode",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Location code of the line."
            },
            {
              "name": "newLocationCode",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "New location code of the line."
            },
            {
              "name": "binCode",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Bin code of the line."
            },
            {
              "name": "newBinCode",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "New bin code of the line."
            },
            {
              "name": "lotNo",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Lot number; empty when the line has no single tracking assignment."
            },
            {
              "name": "newLotNo",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "New lot number."
            },
            {
              "name": "serialNo",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Serial number; empty when the line has no single tracking assignment."
            },
            {
              "name": "newSerialNo",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "New serial number."
            },
            {
              "name": "packageNo",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Package number; empty when the line has no single tracking assignment."
            },
            {
              "name": "newPackageNo",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "New package number."
            },
            {
              "name": "tracking",
              "type": "array",
              "description": "Every item tracking assignment of the line: lotNo, newLotNo, serialNo, newSerialNo, packageNo, newPackageNo and quantityBase."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "entryCount",
          "type": "integer",
          "description": "Total number of captured entries."
        },
        {
          "name": "glEntryCount",
          "type": "integer",
          "description": "Number of captured G/L entries."
        }
      ]
    },
    "errors": [
      {
        "code": "PreconditionFailed",
        "when": "The selected journal contains no lines.",
        "fix": "Select a batch with lines or a valid line subset."
      },
      {
        "code": "NothingToPreview",
        "when": "The preview captured no entry, so the posting would create nothing.",
        "fix": "Check that the lines have a quantity to post."
      },
      {
        "code": "BusinessCentralError",
        "when": "Business Central refused the posting preview; the answer carries its own text.",
        "fix": "Correct the cause in the text and retry."
      },
      {
        "code": "BusinessCentralError",
        "error": "Unsupported journal parameter %1.",
        "when": "A key is sent that this type does not read.",
        "fix": "Remove the key; only the batch selectors and the declared parameters are accepted."
      },
      {
        "code": "BusinessCentralError",
        "error": "Identify one existing journal batch using templateName and batchName or subject TEMPLATE|BATCH or SystemId.",
        "when": "No batch is identified, the selectors name different batches, the subject is neither TEMPLATE|BATCH nor a SystemId, the batch does not exist, or its template is not a Phys. Inventory template or is recurring.",
        "fix": "Identify one existing batch of a non-recurring Phys. Inventory template with consistent selectors."
      },
      {
        "code": "InvalidParameter",
        "when": "The Physical Inventory domain is turned off for this company in Inventory Setup.",
        "fix": "Turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page."
      },
      {
        "code": "PermissionDenied",
        "when": "The caller lacks the item posting permission (Item Posting Gate) or write permission on the item journal.",
        "fix": "Ask an administrator for Item Posting Gate."
      }
    ],
    "effect": {
      "effect": "read",
      "changes": "Nothing is kept. The posting is run as a preview and every entry it creates is rolled back; the journal lines stay as they are.",
      "idempotent": true,
      "permissionSet": "Bifrost Read-Only and Item Posting Gate",
      "writes": false,
      "posts": false,
      "rollback": true
    },
    "metering": {
      "chargeable": true,
      "chargedAs": "message"
    },
    "related": [
      {
        "name": "Inventory.PhysInventory.Check",
        "useInsteadWhen": "Use it to list line problems; it does not simulate the posting."
      },
      {
        "name": "Inventory.PhysInventory.RecordCount",
        "useInsteadWhen": "Use it to change the counted quantities before previewing again."
      },
      {
        "name": "Inventory.PhysInventory.Post",
        "useInsteadWhen": "Use it to post the lines for real."
      }
    ],
    "workflow": {
      "steps": [
        {
          "messageType": "Inventory.PhysInventory.Check",
          "purpose": "Find line problems first."
        },
        {
          "messageType": "Inventory.PhysInventory.PreviewPost",
          "purpose": "See the entries the posting would create; everything is rolled back."
        },
        {
          "messageType": "Inventory.PhysInventory.Post",
          "purpose": "Post the count when the preview is acceptable."
        }
      ]
    },
    "examples": [
      {
        "title": "Preview the posting of the batch DEFAULT",
        "request": {
          "type": "Inventory.PhysInventory.PreviewPost",
          "subject": "PHYS. INV.|DEFAULT"
        },
        "response": {
          "status": "Success",
          "templateName": "PHYS. INV.",
          "batchName": "DEFAULT",
          "linesToPost": 1,
          "rollback": true,
          "preview": [
            {
              "tableId": 32,
              "tableName": "Item Ledger Entry",
              "tableCaption": "Item Ledger Entry",
              "entryCount": 1,
              "entries": [
                {
                  "ItemNo_": "1000"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "totals": {
            "totalDebitLCY": 0,
            "totalCreditLCY": 0
          },
          "result": [
            {
              "systemId": "6f1c1d2e-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
              "lineNo": 10000,
              "itemNo": "1000",
              "quantity": 2
            }
          ],
          "entryCount": 1,
          "glEntryCount": 0
        }
      }
    ],
    "overview": "Runs the posting of one Phys. Inventory journal batch as a preview, returns the entries it would create and rolls everything back. It needs the item posting permission.",
    "notes": "Runs the standard posting preview of the journal lines and rolls it back, so no ledger entry, item register or journal change is kept. rollback is true in every Success answer. The type needs the item posting permission (Item Posting Gate), like Inventory.PhysInventory.Post; without it the call is refused with PermissionDenied. The whole batch is previewed, or only the lines in lineSystemIds. preview lists the captured entries per table; totals carries totalDebitLCY and totalCreditLCY and carries balanced only when G/L entries were captured. A batch without lines is refused with PreconditionFailed. A preview that would create nothing is answered NothingToPreview. An error that the preview raises is answered with code BusinessCentralError and Business Central's own text. Each selected line must be a valid physical inventory line (item set and not blocked, adjustment entry type, Direct Cost value entry type, no item charge); otherwise the call fails with BusinessCentralError. Use Inventory.PhysInventory.Check for a list of line problems."
  },
  "conventions": "## Errors and warnings\r\nAn error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.\r\nWhen a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.\r\nRequest values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.\r\nRequest values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `\"1234.56\"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.\r\nAnswers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.\r\nBoth success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.\r\n`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {\"type\":\"Memory.User.Set\",\"strict\":true,\"data\":{\"memory\":\"test\",\"memry\":\"typo\"}} is refused.\r\n`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.\r\nFeature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.\r\nA message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.\r\n`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is \"no concurrent lock on the same records\"; `nextStep` is \"Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed.\" Bifrost does not retry automatically. Other platform errors, including uncaught queue-path errors, remain `BusinessCentralError`.\r\nCodes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.\r\n"
}
